# Grammar chapters

Authoring source of truth: `content/grammar/GRAMMAR_AUTHORING_GUIDE.md`. Exemplar: Chapter 1.

When drafting or editing a grammar chapter:

- One system per chapter. English contrast first. Piles (he / she / leftover) and last letter before school labels.
- Every teaching block is thesis, two or three full support sentences, then a close. No phrase fragments as sentences.
- Every Bosnian line has a speaker (Ana, Emir, Amira) on `knownLine` and `look.items`.
- `speakTargets` are 0-based indexes into `look.items` (two or three lines). Record yourself sits on that dialogue card. Not on vocab cards. Not AWS jargon in learner copy.
- Vocab is 4–6 tap-to-hear words only.
- Photos: `G.Na` refs, complete-sentence caption, credit links to `/attributions`.
- Parallel handbook. Not Book 2. No civic, cat plot, Lesson A/B, authentic listen, or Cyrillic.
